<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lijiashan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lijiashan is an archaeological cemetery near Jiangchuan in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, belonging to the Dian culture. Excavated from 1972, its tombs, dating from about the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>, yielded bronze drums, weapons, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cowrie-shell">cowrie</a> containers and ornaments, among them the well-known bronze ox-and-tiger table. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shizhaishan">Shizhaishan</a> it is a principal source for the art and society of the Dian kingdom.</p></div>
